     "INC report (session inc-4917-sre-alice)\n========================================\n**Root cause:**  \nThe recent production release `rel\u20112031` (10:02) reduced the checkout\u2011api database connection pool from 50 to **10** and upgraded the ORM. This caused HikariCP to exhaust its pool, leading to ~1800\u202fms wait times, a p95 latency of ~2.14\u202fs, and a 3.9\u202f% error rate.\n\n**Action:**  \nPlan to roll back `checkout\u2011api` from `rel\u20112031` to the previous release `rel\u20112030`. This restores the original pool size and resolves the latency/5xx issue without restarting or scaling the service.\n\n**Verification:**  \nAfter rollback, query `latency_p95_ms` for the last 3\u202fminutes; it must drop below the 400\u202fms SLO. Once verified, update the incident to \u201cmitigated\u201d with a note summarizing the root cause, action taken, and verification result.\n"
